Changelog: 28-11-2026 12:38:25

Fixed. The comments and texts that name an emulator manager use its new name, such as PS5 PCSX2 Manager (owner, 28-11-2026).

Changelog: 28-11-2026 12:17:30

Fixed. The catalog lists the programs that the portal, the apps and core run and that it lacked (owner, 28-11-2026: add them).
It has 51 more tools, 79 in all, and 104 more sources, each found in the code.
Board Test had no tools listed, and now has its own, as the twin lists them.
pkexec is optional for SFTP Tools, not required. The app offers the local SSH server only where systemctl and pkexec are there.
firewall-cmd's description says what the program is, since Board Test uses it too.
Core counts as installed while any app is installed, because every app carries it. Before, core's tools showed as not needed.
The test that each tool is named in the code of each owner reads core/ and portal/ for the owners core and portal.
The test's TOOLS set has the new tools.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 11:51:20

Added. An Emulators section follows the firmware (owner, 28-11-2026). It has a card for each emulator manager: KytyPS5, PCSX2, PPSSPP, RPCS3, shadPS4, Vita3K and Xenia.
A card shows the build the manager was tested with and the latest release on GitHub.
PCSX2, PPSSPP, RPCS3 and shadPS4 are compared with their latest stable release. KytyPS5, Vita3K and Xenia publish builds only.
A newer one stays on the card until a release of the manager has it, and the hourly reminder names it once. Nothing is installed from here.
The pins and repositories are read from each manager's emulator.py by --sync-upstreams, and tests/test_upstreams.py fails while the catalog misses a manager.
This brings back what the change of 28-11-2026 00:38:32 removed, with Nexus's GitHub check: a sign-in with gh raises GitHub's limit from 60 to 5,000 requests an hour.
The Check again button's icon is drawn 1.5 pixels heavier, so it matches the bold Fix beside it (owner, 28-11-2026).

Changelog: 28-11-2026 11:31:59

Added. Nexus Deps is called Nexus Dependencies for PS5 now (owner, 28-11-2026). The window, the menu entry, the notifications and the wiki use that name.
The PS5 system software card and the PlayStation Portal card read the newest version from Sony's system software pages.
A new version there is news once, as on the PS4 card. Both cards were checked on the device before.
Each firmware card's information box links to Sony's pages for it.
The DualSense card links to Sony's steps to update a DualSense on a PC or PS5, and a DualSense Edge on a PC.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 00:38:32

Breaking. Nexus Deps no longer lists the emulators (owner, 28-11-2026). Each emulator manager fetches the versions
from GitHub and installs the one you choose, and that is the only way to choose one. The GitHub cards, their pins
and the check that every emulator app is listed are gone. The window's section is called Firmware now and holds
Sony's firmware cards. `--sync-upstreams` reads only the names and launchers of the apps from `apps.toml`.

